From a6b2f26e787c28716558bc7684551e176094eb47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Medium1992 <Medium1992@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 02:36:37 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] XHTTP: Keep what a limited flow governor stack is shown, wake
 streams the limit refused

A SETTINGS frame that carries no initial window cleared the mark that the
stack is shown one frame; the next credit forwarded the stack what it had
been shown less, and a lowering of the window that could be passed on closed
the connection. The mark now follows only a frame that carries a window.

A lowering under what the stack was forwarded gives the connection up again
where the stack had used all of that: passing it on by showing the stack
nothing left a stream opened then at no window for good.

A stream the send window kept credit from was looked at again only when its
own client returned credit, and one left with less than a client returns
credit for sent nothing that would bring any. Such streams now wait in a
queue and are handed the room that frees, oldest first, in quanta.
